# {{ .Service.Name.Title }} — a solution backend

This service is the entry service of the `{{ .Module.Name.LowerCase }}` solution: the
workload a host installs, built on
[`solution-runtime-go`](https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go).

The runtime does everything a solution needs identically — it presents what the
solution is, answers `/health`, serves the page's calls, and relays the page's
module calls to the authority's hop **as the viewer**, where each module
authorizes the call. What lives here is this solution's own composition:

| file | what it says |
|---|---|
| `main.go` | what the solution is: its id, its contract, its capabilities |
| `operations.go` | the routes this backend serves itself, each with the policy a call must hold |
| `consumes.go` | per consumed module: the authority asked for the viewer, and the methods that may be called |
| `consumed_gen.go` | **generated** from `api.consumes` — `codefly sync` rewrites it |
| `openapi/api.swagger.json` | **generated** from the routes above — `go generate ./...` rewrites it |

A solution reaches every module through the authority's hop, which checks the
call. It therefore declares **no** `service-dependencies` edge on a module it
consumes: Codefly renders such an edge into a mesh allow rule straight to that
module's service, past the check. `consumes_test.go` holds this service to that.

The page this solution serves is `../fe-remote` — the `./Page` Module
Federation remote, an npm package rather than a Codefly service.
